    }
   },
   {
    "field": "special",
    "value": "secreted soluble antibodies",
    "quote": "A plasma cell is a B cell that has differentiated in response to antigen binding, and has thereby gained the ability to secrete soluble antibodies.",
    "source": {
     "section": "21.1 Anatomy of the Lymphatic and Immune Systems",
